#, no-wrap
msgid "Answers to commonly-asked questions about execution modes"
msgstr "Jawapan kepada soalan yang kerap ditanya tentang mod pelaksanaan"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Execution modes FAQs"
msgstr "Soalan lazim mod pelaksanaan"

#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Execution modes FAQs {#execution-modes-faqs}"
msgstr "Soalan lazim mod pelaksanaan {#execution-modes-faqs}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"  <AccordionItem title=\"Does `qiskit-ibm-runtime` local testing mode support different execution modes?\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"  <AccordionItem title=\"Adakah `qiskit-ibm-runtime` mod pengujian setempat menyokong mod pelaksanaan yang berbeza?\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Local testing mode supports the syntax for the different execution modes, but because there is no scheduling involved when testing locally, the modes are ignored.\n"
"  </AccordionItem>\n"
msgstr ""
"Mod pengujian setempat menyokong sintaks untuk mod pelaksanaan yang berbeza, tetapi oleh kerana tiada penjadualan yang terlibat apabila menguji secara setempat, mod-mod tersebut diabaikan.\n"
"  </AccordionItem>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  <span id=\"parallel\"></span>\n"
"  <AccordionItem title=\"How many jobs can run in parallel for a specific backend?\">\n"
msgstr ""
"  <span id=\"parallel\"></span>\n"
"  <AccordionItem title=\"Berapa banyak kerja yang boleh berjalan secara selari untuk backend tertentu?\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The number of jobs running in parallel is based on the degree of parallelism configured for the backend, which is five for most backends today.\n"
"  </AccordionItem>\n"
msgstr ""
"Bilangan kerja yang berjalan secara selari adalah berdasarkan darjat keselarian yang dikonfigurasi untuk backend, iaitu lima untuk kebanyakan backend hari ini.\n"
"  </AccordionItem>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  <AccordionItem title=\"How is usage reported for failed or canceled jobs?\">\n"
msgstr "  <AccordionItem title=\"Bagaimana penggunaan dilaporkan untuk kerja yang gagal atau dibatalkan?\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"See the [Failed and canceled jobs](/guides/estimate-job-run-time#failed-job) section on the Execution modes page.\n"
"  </AccordionItem>\n"
msgstr ""
"Lihat bahagian [Kerja yang gagal dan dibatalkan](/guides/estimate-job-run-time#failed-job) pada halaman Mod pelaksanaan.\n"
"  </AccordionItem>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "</Accordion>\n"
msgstr "</Accordion>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sessions {#sessions}"
msgstr "Sesi {#sessions}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"  <AccordionItem title=\"What happens to my jobs if a session is closed?\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"  <AccordionItem title=\"Apa yang berlaku kepada kerja saya jika sesi ditutup?\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If you are using the `Session` class in `qiskit-ibm-runtime`:\n"
msgstr "Jika anda menggunakan kelas `Session` dalam `qiskit-ibm-runtime`:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`Session.close()` means the session no longer accepts new jobs, but existing jobs run to completion.\n"
msgstr "`Session.close()` bermakna sesi tidak lagi menerima kerja baharu, tetapi kerja yang sedia ada dijalankan sehingga selesai.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`Session.cancel()` cancels all pending session jobs.\n"
msgstr "`Session.cancel()` membatalkan semua kerja sesi yang belum selesai.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If you are using the REST API directly:\n"
msgstr "Jika anda menggunakan REST API secara langsung:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`PATCH /sessions/{id}` with `accepting_jobs=False` means the session no longer accepts new jobs, but existing jobs run to completion.\n"
msgstr "`PATCH /sessions/{id}` dengan `accepting_jobs=False` bermakna sesi tidak lagi menerima kerja baharu, tetapi kerja yang sedia ada dijalankan sehingga selesai.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  - `DELETE /sessions/{id}/close` cancels all pending session jobs.\n"
"  </AccordionItem>\n"
msgstr ""
"  - `DELETE /sessions/{id}/close` membatalkan semua kerja sesi yang belum selesai.\n"
"  </AccordionItem>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  <AccordionItem title=\"If I am using session mode and expect my experiment to take many hours, is there a way to ask for calibrations to happen?\">\n"
msgstr "  <AccordionItem title=\"Jika saya menggunakan mod sesi dan menjangkakan eksperimen saya akan mengambil masa berjam-jam, adakah terdapat cara untuk meminta kalibrasi berlaku?\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"No. On-demand calibration is not available.\n"
"  </AccordionItem>\n"
msgstr ""
"Tidak. Kalibrasi atas permintaan tidak tersedia.\n"
"  </AccordionItem>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  <AccordionItem title=\"Is there an interactive timeout (interactive TTL) with session mode?\">\n"
msgstr "  <AccordionItem title=\"Adakah terdapat tamat masa interaktif (TTL interaktif) dengan mod sesi?\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Yes. This reduces unwanted cost if a user forgets to close their session.\n"
"  </AccordionItem>\n"
msgstr ""
"Ya. Ini mengurangkan kos yang tidak diingini jika pengguna terlupa menutup sesi mereka.\n"
"  </AccordionItem>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  <AccordionItem title=\"Can I change the interactive TTL or the maximum TTL of a session?\">\n"
msgstr "  <AccordionItem title=\"Bolehkah saya menukar TTL interaktif atau TTL maksimum sesi?\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You cannot change the interactive TTL value. You can change the maximum TTL value of a session (see [Specify the session length](/guides/run-jobs-session#specify-length)), but it must be less than the system-defined maximum. Ask your administrator to contact IBM support if you need a different interactive TTL or system maximum TTL.\n"
msgstr "Anda tidak boleh menukar nilai TTL interaktif. Anda boleh menukar nilai TTL maksimum sesi (lihat [Tentukan tempoh sesi](/guides/run-jobs-session#specify-length)), tetapi ia mesti kurang daripada maksimum yang ditakrifkan sistem. Minta pentadbir anda untuk menghubungi sokongan IBM jika anda memerlukan TTL interaktif atau TTL maksimum sistem yang berbeza.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  </AccordionItem>\n"
msgstr "  </AccordionItem>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  <AccordionItem title=\"How does session usage impact IBM Quantum Network members who are not billed by usage?\">\n"
msgstr "  <AccordionItem title=\"Bagaimana penggunaan sesi mempengaruhi ahli IBM Quantum Network yang tidak dikenakan bayaran mengikut penggunaan?\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"IBM Quantum Network members gain reserved capacity on IBM Quantum&reg; QPUs. Usage is deducted from this capacity and instances with lower capacity have longer queueing time.\n"
"  </AccordionItem>\n"
msgstr ""
"Ahli IBM Quantum Network mendapat kapasiti rizab pada QPU IBM Quantum&reg;. Penggunaan ditolak dari kapasiti ini dan instans dengan kapasiti yang lebih rendah mempunyai masa beratur yang lebih lama.\n"
"  </AccordionItem>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  <AccordionItem title=\"Do I get the same parallelism in session mode that I get with batch mode?\">\n"
msgstr "  <AccordionItem title=\"Adakah saya mendapat keselarian yang sama dalam mod sesi seperti yang saya dapat dengan mod batch?\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Yes. If you submit multiple jobs simultaneously in a session, these jobs will run in parallel.\n"
"  </AccordionItem>\n"
msgstr ""
"Ya. Jika anda menghantar berbilang kerja serentak dalam sesi, kerja-kerja ini akan berjalan secara selari.\n"
"  </AccordionItem>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  <AccordionItem title=\"Can sessions be interrupted by QPU upgrades or calibrations?\">\n"
msgstr "  <AccordionItem title=\"Bolehkah sesi diganggu oleh naik taraf QPU atau kalibrasi?\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"No.  Sessions run in dedicated mode, which means that the user has total access to the backend.  Sessions are never interrupted by calibrations or software upgrades.\n"
"  </AccordionItem>\n"
msgstr ""
"Tidak. Sesi berjalan dalam mod khusus, bermakna pengguna mempunyai akses penuh kepada backend. Sesi tidak pernah diganggu oleh kalibrasi atau naik taraf perisian.\n"
"  </AccordionItem>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  <AccordionItem title=\"Is compilation time counted as usage in session mode?\">\n"
msgstr "  <AccordionItem title=\"Adakah masa kompilasi dikira sebagai penggunaan dalam mod sesi?\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Yes.  In session mode, usage is the wall clock time the QPU is **committed to the session**. It starts when the first session job starts and ends when the session goes inactive, is closed, or when the last job completes, whichever happens **last**. Thus, usage continues to accumulate after a session ends if the QPU is still running a job. Additionally, time after a job completes while the QPU waits for another session job (the interactive TTL) counts as usage. This is why you should ensure the session is closed as soon as you are done submitting jobs to it.\n"
"  </AccordionItem>\n"
msgstr ""
"Ya. Dalam mod sesi, penggunaan adalah masa jam dinding QPU **ditetapkan untuk sesi**. Ia bermula apabila kerja sesi pertama bermula dan berakhir apabila sesi menjadi tidak aktif, ditutup, atau apabila kerja terakhir selesai, mana yang berlaku **terakhir**. Oleh itu, penggunaan terus terkumpul selepas sesi berakhir jika QPU masih menjalankan kerja. Selain itu, masa selepas kerja selesai sementara QPU menunggu kerja sesi lain (TTL interaktif) dikira sebagai penggunaan. Inilah sebabnya anda harus memastikan sesi ditutup sebaik sahaja anda selesai menghantar kerja ke dalamnya.\n"
"  </AccordionItem>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Batch {#batch}"
msgstr "Batch {#batch}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"  <AccordionItem title=\"How many jobs run in parallel in batch mode?\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"  <AccordionItem title=\"Berapa banyak kerja yang berjalan secara selari dalam mod batch?\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The number of jobs running in parallel is based on the degree of parallelism configured for the backend, which is five for most backends. However, the number of concurrent jobs in an active batch could be lower because there could be other jobs already running when the batch becomes active.\n"
"  </AccordionItem>\n"
msgstr ""
"Bilangan kerja yang berjalan secara selari adalah berdasarkan darjat keselarian yang dikonfigurasi untuk backend, iaitu lima untuk kebanyakan backend. Namun, bilangan kerja serentak dalam batch aktif boleh lebih rendah kerana mungkin ada kerja lain yang sudah berjalan apabila batch menjadi aktif.\n"
"  </AccordionItem>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  <AccordionItem title=\"How is running _N_ PUBs in job mode different from running _N_ single-PUB jobs in batch mode?\">\n"
msgstr "  <AccordionItem title=\"Apa perbezaan antara menjalankan _N_ PUB dalam mod kerja berbanding menjalankan _N_ kerja satu PUB dalam mod batch?\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The main difference is the time and cost tradeoff:\n"
msgstr "Perbezaan utamanya ialah pertukaran masa dan kos:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Batch mode:\n"
msgstr "Mod batch:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The total run time is less because the classical processing might run in parallel.\n"
msgstr "Jumlah masa jalankan adalah lebih singkat kerana pemprosesan klasik mungkin berjalan secara selari.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "There is a slight overhead for running each job, so you end up paying a little more for batched jobs versus when all circuits are executed in a single job.\n"
msgstr "Terdapat sedikit overhead untuk menjalankan setiap kerja, jadi anda akhirnya membayar sedikit lebih untuk kerja yang dibatch berbanding apabila semua litar dilaksanakan dalam satu kerja sahaja.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because batch mode doesn't give you exclusive access to a backend, jobs inside a batch might run with other users' jobs or calibration jobs.\n"
msgstr "Oleh kerana mod batch tidak memberi anda akses eksklusif kepada backend, kerja dalam batch mungkin berjalan bersama kerja pengguna lain atau kerja kalibrasi.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "If some jobs fail, you still get results from the completed jobs.\n"
msgstr "Jika beberapa kerja gagal, anda masih mendapat keputusan dari kerja yang selesai.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can take action in the middle of a batch workload based on the results of completed jobs. For example, you can cancel the rest of the jobs if the initial results look incorrect.\n"
msgstr "Anda boleh mengambil tindakan di tengah-tengah beban kerja batch berdasarkan keputusan kerja yang selesai. Contohnya, anda boleh membatalkan kerja selebihnya jika keputusan awal kelihatan tidak betul.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Job mode:\n"
msgstr "Mod kerja:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The total run time is likely to be higher because there is no parallelism.\n"
msgstr "Jumlah masa jalankan kemungkinan lebih tinggi kerana tiada keselarian.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "You don't pay for the extra per-job overhead associated with batch workloads.\n"
msgstr "Anda tidak membayar overhead setiap kerja yang berkaitan dengan beban kerja batch.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "All of your circuits will run together.\n"
msgstr "Semua litar anda akan berjalan bersama.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "If this single job fails, you don't get partial results.\n"
msgstr "Jika kerja tunggal ini gagal, anda tidak mendapat keputusan separa.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Your job might hit the limit if it contains too many circuits or if the circuits are too large.\n"
msgstr "Kerja anda mungkin mencapai had jika mengandungi terlalu banyak litar atau jika litar terlalu besar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In general, if your each of your jobs consumes less than a minute of QPU time, consider combining them into a larger job (this applies to all execution modes).\n"
"  </AccordionItem>\n"
msgstr ""
"Secara umum, jika setiap kerja anda menggunakan kurang daripada satu minit masa QPU, pertimbangkan untuk menggabungkannya menjadi kerja yang lebih besar (ini terpakai untuk semua mod pelaksanaan).\n"
"  </AccordionItem>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  <AccordionItem title=\"How many jobs I can submit in a batch?\">\n"
msgstr "  <AccordionItem title=\"Berapa banyak kerja yang boleh saya hantar dalam batch?\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"While there are no limits to the number of jobs you can submit in a batch, there is a maximum time associated with a batch. That is, when a batch's wall clock time (which starts when the first batch job starts running) exceeds the system-defined maximum time, the batch will not accept any new jobs, and any jobs queued but not running are canceled. Additionally, there are limits on how much usage your jobs can consume based on your plan. To determine the maximum time associated with a batch, use the [`batch.details()`  method](/guides/run-jobs-batch#batch-details) and look for the `max_time` value.\n"
"  </AccordionItem>\n"
msgstr ""
"Walaupun tiada had pada bilangan kerja yang boleh anda hantar dalam batch, terdapat masa maksimum yang dikaitkan dengan batch. Iaitu, apabila masa jam dinding batch (yang bermula apabila kerja batch pertama mula berjalan) melebihi masa maksimum yang ditakrifkan sistem, batch tidak akan menerima sebarang kerja baharu, dan sebarang kerja dalam barisan tetapi tidak berjalan dibatalkan. Selain itu, terdapat had pada berapa banyak penggunaan yang boleh digunakan oleh kerja anda berdasarkan pelan anda. Untuk menentukan masa maksimum yang dikaitkan dengan batch, gunakan [kaedah `batch.details()`](/guides/run-jobs-batch#batch-details) dan cari nilai `max_time`.\n"
"  </AccordionItem>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  <AccordionItem title=\"When would my batch mode jobs run in parallel with other users' jobs?\">\n"
msgstr "  <AccordionItem title=\"Bila kerja mod batch saya akan berjalan secara selari dengan kerja pengguna lain?\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The degree of parallelism configured for a backend is also called \"execution lanes\". If there are one or more execution lanes available, and your batch jobs are next in line to be run, the scheduler starts enough jobs to fill the lanes. Similarly, if your batch doesn't have enough jobs to fill the lanes, the scheduler starts other users' jobs.\n"
msgstr "Darjat keselarian yang dikonfigurasi untuk backend juga disebut \"lorong pelaksanaan\". Jika terdapat satu atau lebih lorong pelaksanaan yang tersedia, dan kerja batch anda berada dalam barisan seterusnya untuk dijalankan, penjadual memulakan kerja yang cukup untuk mengisi lorong. Begitu juga, jika batch anda tidak mempunyai kerja yang cukup untuk mengisi lorong, penjadual memulakan kerja pengguna lain.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Example: The backend you choose has five execution lanes, and two of them are currently occupied by other users' jobs. Your batch of six jobs is next in line to be run.\n"
msgstr "Contoh: Backend yang anda pilih mempunyai lima lorong pelaksanaan, dan dua daripadanya sedang diduduki oleh kerja pengguna lain. Batch anda yang mengandungi enam kerja berada dalam barisan seterusnya untuk dijalankan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Because there are three available lanes, the scheduler starts three of your six batch jobs. It continues to start jobs in your batch as jobs finish and execution lanes become available. If a lane becomes available and there are no more jobs in your batch, the scheduler starts the next job in line.\n"
"  </AccordionItem>\n"
msgstr ""
"Oleh kerana terdapat tiga lorong yang tersedia, penjadual memulakan tiga daripada enam kerja batch anda. Ia terus memulakan kerja dalam batch anda apabila kerja selesai dan lorong pelaksanaan tersedia. Jika lorong tersedia dan tiada lagi kerja dalam batch anda, penjadual memulakan kerja seterusnya dalam barisan.\n"
"  </AccordionItem>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  <AccordionItem title=\"Do all of my batch jobs need to wait in the queue?\">\n"
msgstr "  <AccordionItem title=\"Adakah semua kerja batch saya perlu menunggu dalam barisan?\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Because QPUs are limited and shared resources, all jobs need to wait in the queue. However, when the first job in your batch starts running, all the other jobs in that batch essentially jump to the front of the queue and are prioritized by the scheduler.\n"
"  </AccordionItem>\n"
msgstr ""
"Oleh kerana QPU adalah sumber terhad dan dikongsi, semua kerja perlu menunggu dalam barisan. Walau bagaimanapun, apabila kerja pertama dalam batch anda mula berjalan, semua kerja lain dalam batch tersebut pada dasarnya melompat ke hadapan barisan dan diutamakan oleh penjadual.\n"
"  </AccordionItem>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  <AccordionItem title=\"Does a batch end automatically when the last associated job ends?\">\n"
msgstr "  <AccordionItem title=\"Adakah batch berakhir secara automatik apabila kerja terakhir yang berkaitan selesai?\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Yes. However, there is a slight overhead associated with this auto-detection, so you should always close your batch and session.\n"
"  </AccordionItem>\n"
msgstr ""
"Ya. Walau bagaimanapun, terdapat sedikit overhead yang dikaitkan dengan pengesanan automatik ini, jadi anda harus sentiasa menutup batch dan sesi anda.\n"
"  </AccordionItem>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  <AccordionItem title=\"Can batches be interrupted by calibrations or software upgrades\">\n"
msgstr "  <AccordionItem title=\"Bolehkah batch diganggu oleh kalibrasi atau naik taraf perisian\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Yes.  Batch workloads might be interrupted by calibrations or software upgrades.\n"
"  </AccordionItem>\n"
msgstr ""
"Ya. Beban kerja batch mungkin diganggu oleh kalibrasi atau naik taraf perisian.\n"
"  </AccordionItem>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  <AccordionItem title=\"Is compilation time counted as usage in batch mode?\">\n"
msgstr "  <AccordionItem title=\"Adakah masa kompilasi dikira sebagai penggunaan dalam mod batch?\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"No.  In batch mode, only time spent on the quantum hardware counts as usage.\n"
"  </AccordionItem>\n"
msgstr ""
"Tidak. Dalam mod batch, hanya masa yang dihabiskan pada perkakasan kuantum dikira sebagai penggunaan.\n"
"  </AccordionItem>\n"
